Single arm, 75 lines, clippy 0, critique.rs only.

Sets all three of XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME and XDG_CACHE_HOME on the spawned
command, per run. fb critique previously set NONE of them, so every critique run
used the shared ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db -- 275MB -- and fb critique
starts up to FB_SLOTS arms concurrently against it. That is the exact contention
that deadlocked three processes in farmerbob-p3r.

The arm separated the path computation from the spawn, as the spec asked, so the
isolation is tested without launching a real agent.

